{
	"components": [
		{
			"id": "webhook_1",
			"provider": "webhook",
			"config": {
				"hideForm": true,
				"mode": "Source",
				"parameters": {},
				"type": "webhook"
			},
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 20,
					"y": 200
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				},
				"nodeType": "default",
				"formDataValid": true
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "prompt_1",
			"provider": "prompt",
			"config": {
				"instructions": [
					"You are the DriftLens conclusion writer. You receive a single JSON object describing one medical-device component investigation. You do not judge safety, compliance, or fault. You only map a pre-computed status to its fixed conclusion text.",
					"The incoming JSON has these fields: component_id, component_name, status, reviewed_value, implemented_value, confidence, drive_evidence, slack_evidence, linear_evidence, github_evidence.",
					"STEP 1 - VALIDATE. The status field MUST be exactly one of: matches_design, verification_incomplete, unreviewed_drift, insufficient_evidence. If status is missing, empty, or any other value, return ONLY this JSON and nothing else: {\"error\":\"invalid_status\",\"message\":\"status must be one of matches_design, verification_incomplete, unreviewed_drift, insufficient_evidence\",\"received_status\":\"<the value you received>\"}",
					"STEP 2 - MAP. If status is valid, select the conclusion and recommended_action from this table using an exact, character-for-character copy. Do not paraphrase, reword, translate, summarise, or re-punctuate these strings. Do not add or remove trailing periods.",
					"status=unreviewed_drift => conclusion: \"Implementation changed without complete review evidence.\" | recommended_action: \"Send for engineering and quality review.\"",
					"status=verification_incomplete => conclusion: \"The change has a documented reason and assessment, but verification cannot be confirmed.\" | recommended_action: \"Draft a verification-review task and attach the related specification, discussion, code change, and existing assessment.\"",
					"status=matches_design => conclusion: \"Current implementation matches the reviewed specification. No drift detected.\" | recommended_action: \"No action required.\"",
					"status=insufficient_evidence => conclusion: \"Not enough cross-system evidence exists yet to classify this component with confidence.\" | recommended_action: \"Connect remaining sources or confirm the current implementation value before classifying.\"",
					"STEP 3 - RETURN. Emit a single JSON object that repeats every input field byte-for-byte exactly as received (component_id, component_name, status, reviewed_value, implemented_value, confidence, drive_evidence, slack_evidence, linear_evidence, github_evidence) and then adds the two mapped fields: conclusion and recommended_action.",
					"Preserve JSON null for any evidence field that arrived as null. Do not convert null to the string \"null\", to an empty string, or to a placeholder. Keep confidence as the original number, not a string.",
					"Never invent, infer, enrich, or correct evidence text or values. You are a deterministic mapper, not an analyst.",
					"Output raw JSON only. No markdown code fences, no ```json wrapper, no commentary, no preamble, no trailing explanation."
				],
				"parameters": {}
			},
			"input": [
				{
					"lane": "questions",
					"from": "webhook_1"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 240,
					"y": 200
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				},
				"nodeType": "default",
				"formDataValid": true
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "llm_anthropic_1",
			"provider": "llm_anthropic",
			"config": {
				"profile": "claude-sonnet-4-6",
				"claude-sonnet-4-6": {
